<title>USA: ARCO lowers posted crude prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>ARCO lowers posted crude prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlantic Richfield Co. said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Thursday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $19.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.00 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $19.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $19.25.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
